  "body": "Historical composition fixtures lost their Git comparison context and immutable apps objects, while newer native feeds invalidated old fixture versions and dates. Preserve genuine object closure in disposable copies, commit explicit synthetic fixture states, and make historical scenarios declare the old pin they exercise. Inventory fixtures are labeled synthetic and cannot replace native scan evidence. Switching assertions use each signed edge's date; the unsigned legacy CVE case also retains the genuinely published major ahead.\n\nOSCAL claim linting now reads policy members from the shared machinery renderer, so current optional machinery resolves and unrelated names still fail. New regressions cover committed apps history, excluded dirty bytes, actual machinery discovery, unknown members and an omitted optional rung. Production composition functions, native inventory guards, converters and every frozen policy body are preserved.\n\nValidation: genuine assembled full composition selfcheck; 103 composition tests; 13 inventory/CVE guards; two machinery tests; public feed and OSCAL verifiers; clean signed source and full-index patch reverse-apply check. Earlier failed historical fixture iterations remain separately recorded. This change does not alter prices, grades, primary clocks, live declarations or the historical coverage floor.\n",
